Subject: Cantor Semantic Inspection Consumer Handoff P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 8a0b1a33-e4fb-432c-8b8d-c59363e67153
@ [specification_uuid] 6abf0365-921b-4d9c-a794-a65ae187ffae

& [WisdomPass]
  + candidate pure consumer acceptance plus golden portable handoff
  + support published wire and one-shot host with exact replay; independently owned Scribe needs explicit consumable contract
  + fit moves verified semantic engine toward an application dependency without duplicating application work
  + disposition proceed_with_smallest_pure_boundary

& [CautionPass]
  + candidate subprocess wrappers can silently become general launchers or misidentify arbitrary binaries
  + missing_support installed application launch policy and executable-identity authority
  + cost one pure crate small fixtures and bounded development harness rather than a resident service
  + hidden_constraint EOF framing is not MCP stdio framing and exit0 can contain semantic refusal
  + failure_path accepting partial output or trusting a self-sealed response without replay would produce false acceptance
  + truth_test adversarial transcript mutations and fresh-process golden replay through the existing host
  + disposition permit_pure_verifier_and_development_proof_only

& [MergeDisposition]
  + contract digest exact byte receipts and separate failure classes are timely supported integration work
  + executable identity installed consumer application admission and MCP are explicitly unresolved outside
  + review_trigger an application-specific accepted launch contract or separately signed MCP successor
